James inquired about adding a "loading" graphic over a Leaflet map in a Shiny application while new data loads. I provided a comprehensive solution encompassing CSS for a loading spinner, JavaScript for toggling spinner visibility, and modifications needed in Shiny's UI and server functions. The steps included creating an elegant loading graphic styled with CSS, integrating JavaScript to control the spinner's display using custom messages from Shiny, and ensuring the spinner appears during the data loading process. Ultimately, this setup allows for a smoother user experience, keeping users informed while they wait for the map to refresh with new data.
